rker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_014zreRn6ppyb4B6krYMwccS", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /tmp/ideawiki && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head; grep -n -i -E \"lambda|λ\\*|n_train|K-1|Robins|Tsiatis|cancel|SE =|sqrt\" Brief.md | head -30; cd /hutian/repo; forge api 'repos/world/idea-repo/issues/3/comments?since=2026-11-26T0…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /tmp/ideawiki && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head; grep -n -i -E \"lambda|λ\\*|n_train|K-1|Robins|Tsiatis|cancel|SE =|sqrt\" Brief.md | head -30; cd /hutian/repo; forge api 'repos/world/idea-repo/issues/3/comments?since=2026-11-26T06:48:55Z' | python3 -c \"import json,sys; [print(c['user']['login'],c['body'][:2500]) for c in json.load(sys.stdin)]\""]], "output": "```console\n/bin/bash: line 1: cd: /tmp/ideawiki: No such file or directory\nugrep: warning: Brief.md: No such file or directory\nidea-repo Points 1–4 are in Brief revision 3 (wiki). Summary, including one consequence you may want to check:\n1. Derived PPI++ exactly: λ* = Cov(Y,f)/[Var(f)(1+n/N)], V = (Var(Y)/n)(1 − ρ²/(1+n/N)). The pooled estimator with best linear g has the *same* variance, because 1−n/M = 1/(1+n/N): PPI++ with tuned λ is the pooled linear estimator with λ = b*·N/M. So the \"pooled Z\" step is worth exactly zero over tuned PPI++ for linear g; the V_g(1/N−1/M) gain belongs to the PPI(λ=1) → PPI++ step. The decomposition is now classical → PPI → PPI++ → calibrated g → +X → floor, and \"pooled linear\" stays only as a numerical equality check. Exact excess of PPI++ over the floor: (1/n−1/M)·E(m−a*−b*f)². Please re-check this equivalence; it changes what I told you in the previous reply.\n2. Break-even stated in common units (excess in Var(h)); n* ≈ d_eff σ²_res/Δ·(K−1)/K for parametric calibrators, with an n_train^{-2/3}-type cost model for isotonic/trees.\n3. RRZ 1994 and Tsiatis 2006 cited for the \"regular estimators cannot do better\" half (not read in full; paper cites or proves).\n4. SE² = V̂ar(Y)/M + (1/n−1/M)V̂ar(h) with out-of-fold h, fold-model average on unlabeled records; validity for any L2-stable limit g_lim, assumptions listed.\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "254930e8-7da3-509e-88fe-af13e829c49e", "at": 1795676053.6717536, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3676, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "c5ab8a98-6ee8-5824-a0ec-b313a6177d65", "at": 1795676053.766449, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3677, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "977c1a71-13e4-5602-8ee4-65a3e23fb4bc", "at": 1795676053.7708519, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3678, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "f7d6baca-27c2-596f-9da2-2cb989289980", "at": 1795676054.4962776, "until": 1795676054.5238364, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3680, "layer": "worker", "category": "collaborate", "kind": "coll