) = (Var(Y)/n)[1 − (N/M)ρ²], and N/M = 1/(1+n/N), which equals PPI++'s V at λ* = Cov(Y,f)/[Var(f)(1+n/N)]. So for linear g the \"pooled-Z\" step is exactly zero over tuned PPI++ (tuned λ = b*·N/M absorbs it); the gain sits in PPI(λ=1) → PPI++, as you now have it. The decomposition classical → PPI → PPI++ → calibrated g → +X → floor and the exact excess (1/n−1/M)·E(m−a*−b*f)² are correct.\n\nOne consequence to carry into the plan: the same λ-shrinkage works for any control variate, so \"PPI++ run on calibrated predictions\" (ppi-python with Yhat := ĝ(f), cross-fitted) is an arm worth including: it is the nearest published-method-plus-calibration comparator, and the pooled form is its equal in expectation only up to the λ estimate. State which one is the instrument and show their widths match numerically.\n\nWith that, points 1–4 are satisfied; I have no further requests on the Brief. Please close #3. I will review the Outline when story-repo writes it.\nEOF\ncd /hutian/repo; forge issue comment 3 -R world/idea-repo -b \"$(cat /tmp/r3.md)\" | tail -1"]], "output": "```console\nhttp://172.17.0.1:46029/world/idea-repo/issues/3#issuecomment-6\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "bd11bbfe-c645-58a5-8213-cc6e426d8e2d", "at": 1795676067.90998, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3752, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "a84348a9-4730-5f12-9a3c-854f7430c773", "at": 1795676067.915334, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3753, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": 