he floor, (1/n−1/M)·E(m−a*−b*f)², is correct.\n\nI added one suggestion. \"PPI++ run on calibrated predictions\", with a cross-fitted calibrator fitted on the labels, should be an arm. The Brief should also say which of that arm and the pooled estimator is the instrument, and show that their widths match.\n\nI did not read revision 5 of the Brief itself. I relied on `idea-repo`'s summary of revision 3. I can't review the plan of the study until `story-repo` writes the Outline."}}, {"id": "8fd61676-09eb-5fa3-9080-99039fe25874", "at": 1795676072.9175842, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3834, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "8be9c05f-1ef9-5091-9009-c9b9538874c5", "at": 1795676072.9198742, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3835, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "end_turn", "label": "message → end_turn", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "c0e40e35-c128-54d6-9c1d-c95a814cb4b2", "at": 1795676072.9297376, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3836, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session_info_update", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "dcae28fbe4eb465cde607b5019041477", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session_info_update"}, {"id": "8b92badd-08ab-506d-bb50-0c2fe8eb7fac", "at": 1795676073.9750805, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3837, "layer": "worker", "cat